"""Tests for scripts/extract_info.py.

Fixtures below are real excerpts from /usr/share/info/emacs/*.info.gz
(gzip-decompressed, embedded verbatim as string literals so the tests
stay hermetic and do not depend on /usr/share/info being present):

  - PREAMBLE, EMACS_TOP: emacs.info.gz preamble and the real Top node
    (header + intro prose + a Texinfo menu with group labels and a
    "-- The Detailed Node Listing --" divider).
  - ORG_TOP: org.info.gz's real Top node (same menu shape, different
    manual, per project memory blk_parser_corpus_samples).
  - VISITING: emacs.info.gz's real Visiting node - prose, no menu at all.
  - OTHER_INPUT: emacs.info.gz's real Other Input node - a menu with
    nothing real after it (body should end up empty).
  - CCMODE_CONFIG_BASICS: ccmode.info.gz's real Config Basics node - a
    menu followed by a real Footnotes block (must be kept).
  - ELISP_AUTOLOAD: elisp.info.gz's real Autoload node - a menu followed
    by an ordinary real prose paragraph (must be kept).
  - CALC_EXCERPT: calc.info.gz's real "foo ( # )" line, the one place in
    the whole 66-file corpus that looks like a markdown heading.
  - HELP_NAMES: info.info.gz's real node names in file order; "Help" and
    "Help-]" both slug to "help", the one real collision in the corpus.
  - AUTH_*: auth.info.gz's real Tag Table / End Tag Table / Local
    Variables trailer, and its real Index / Function Index / Variable
    Index nodes (all names ending "Index" must be skipped).
"""

